text:
@brief How long after boot a CHANGE of quality or of program health is
bring-up rather than news, and so is adopted without a log line. Keep it
past the slowest poll rung, so a row is adopted at its first real
reading and not at its default.
@note Alarms are NOT quiet here. This is the change log; a condition
that matters raises its own row and annunciates on its own dwell.

@brief How long a cleared alarm stays in the ALARMS page's RECENT view
(s). A condition's own recent_s overrides it (0 = this default, < 0 =
never expires); the platform alarms in vars.cpp all set their own.

@brief How often the alarm controller sweeps its sources. Dwell times are
in SECONDS, so this only has to be fine enough that an on_s/off_s boundary
lands on the right side.

@brief How often HealthMonitor takes the platform's vitals and produces the
watchdog verdict. Slower than the beat because every input it reads is a
rolling average over many of them.
